WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:17.674
Izzie squeezed Nina's hand and smiled.

2
00:00:17.675 --> 00:00:21.676
She loved to go to the woods during summer camp.

3
00:00:21.677 --> 00:00:24.395
Today the campers had a mission.

4
00:00:24.396 --> 00:00:27.405
They were looking for wildflowers!

5
00:00:27.406 --> 00:00:31.846
"How do we know what to pick?" Izzie asked.

6
00:00:31.847 --> 00:00:36.332
"We don't want to pick flowers growing on a vine or bush.

7
00:00:36.333 --> 00:00:41.321
So look for flowers growing on the ground from one stem.

8
00:00:41.322 --> 00:00:46.572
Big flowers with thick petals will be best," Mr. Dunn said.

9
00:00:46.573 --> 00:00:50.198
"Is this one good?" Bobby asked.

10
00:00:50.199 --> 00:00:56.607
Bobby pointed to a white flower the size of a fingernail.

11
00:00:56.608 --> 00:00:59.635
"No, silly," said Izzie.

12
00:00:59.636 --> 00:01:03.242
"You need something bigger and darker, right, Mr. Dunn?"

13
00:01:03.243 --> 00:01:07.611
The teacher nodded.

14
00:01:07.612 --> 00:01:17.409
"Nina, look at this!" Izzie squatted next to two purple flowers.

15
00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:20.101
"Oh, they're so pretty!

16
00:01:20.102 --> 00:01:23.770
I love the color," Nina gushed.

17
00:01:23.771 --> 00:01:27.437
"Can we pick these, Mr. Dunn?" Izzie asked.

18
00:01:27.438 --> 00:01:32.357
"You may. Those look perfect," said Mr. Dunn.

19
00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:36.637
The girls each picked one.

20
00:01:36.638 --> 00:01:39.729
"Here are some!" Jason called.

21
00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:43.696
He pointed to the same kind of flowers Izzie had found.

22
00:01:43.697 --> 00:01:45.958
But his were bright yellow.

23
00:01:45.959 --> 00:01:48.397
And there were only three of them.

24
00:01:48.398 --> 00:01:51.892
Izzie rushed over, pushing Jason aside.

25
00:01:51.893 --> 00:01:54.482
"Let me get one!"

26
00:01:54.483 --> 00:01:58.313
"Izzie." She felt a firm hand on her arm.

27
00:01:58.314 --> 00:02:04.368
"This is not a competition, and we do not push," Mr. Dunn said.

28
00:02:04.369 --> 00:02:13.176
"Sorry." Izzie watched grumpily as Jason, Ethan, and Bobby picked their flowers.

29
00:02:13.177 --> 00:02:17.798
"Jackpot!" Ethan cried.

30
00:02:17.799 --> 00:02:20.890
He pointed to a small circle of color.

31
00:02:20.891 --> 00:02:27.643
It was made up of flowers—dark purple, light purple, and yellow flowers!

32
00:02:27.644 --> 00:02:31.833
"You only need two flowers," Mr. Dunn said.

33
00:02:31.834 --> 00:02:34.380
"Don't pick more than that.

34
00:02:34.381 --> 00:02:38.958
Flowers are living plants, and their home is here in nature."

35
00:02:38.959 --> 00:02:44.086
But Izzie ignored him.

36
00:02:44.087 --> 00:02:50.519
Quickly she picked six flowers.

37
00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:55.061
Back in the gym, everyone placed their flowers on the table.

38
00:02:55.062 --> 00:02:56.755
Izzie had seven.

39
00:02:56.756 --> 00:02:59.420
Everyone else had two.

40
00:02:59.421 --> 00:03:04.525
"We're going to make hammered flower artwork," said Mr. Dunn.

41
00:03:04.526 --> 00:03:08.735
"I'll explain as we work.

42
00:03:08.736 --> 00:03:13.371
I gave everyone two pieces of watercolor paper.

43
00:03:13.372 --> 00:03:18.486
So you can only use two flowers," said Mr. Dunn.

44
00:03:18.487 --> 00:03:22.348
He looked at Izzie sharply, and then continued.

45
00:03:22.349 --> 00:03:25.994
"Place one flower on the watercolor paper.

46
00:03:25.995 --> 00:03:29.736
Then place a paper towel on top.

47
00:03:29.737 --> 00:03:35.720
Using your hammer, gently pound your flower.

48
00:03:35.721 --> 00:03:42.547
Then lift up the paper towel to see what's left," Mr. Dunn continued.

49
00:03:42.548 --> 00:03:50.746
Izzie chose her favorite flower and began pounding.

50
00:03:50.747 --> 00:03:56.164
When she pulled back her paper towel, she gasped.

51
00:03:56.165 --> 00:03:59.847
"It looks like a stamp," Izzie exclaimed.

52
00:03:59.848 --> 00:04:02.369
"But also like a painting!"

53
00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:07.475
Suddenly she felt bad for picking more flowers than she needed.

54
00:04:07.476 --> 00:04:10.408
"Mr. Dunn?" she said.

55
00:04:10.409 --> 00:04:13.882
"I'm sorry I didn't listen to you.

56
00:04:13.883 --> 00:04:18.524
Can I put my extra flowers in water so they don't die right away?"

57
00:04:18.525 --> 00:04:20.597
Mr. Dunn nodded.

58
00:04:20.598 --> 00:04:25.353
"I'm sure you'll be a better listener next time," he said.

59
00:04:25.354 --> 00:04:28.924
"I'll put the flowers in water.

60
00:04:28.925 --> 00:04:32.222
You can keep working on your hammered artwork.

61
00:04:32.223 --> 00:04:34.256
It looks great."

62
00:04:34.257 --> 00:04:37.453
"Thanks," said Izzie.

63
00:04:37.454 --> 00:04:42.020
Izzie carefully picked off a piece of petal that was stuck to the paper.

64
00:04:42.021 --> 00:04:44.595
Mr. Dunn was so nice.

65
00:04:44.596 --> 00:04:49.069
Izzie knew just what to do with her hammered artwork when it was ready.

66
00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:56.126
She was going to give it to Mr. Dunn!
